### **Logical Relationships**

- **G1 -> G2, G7, G8 [AND][;]**  
  The overall goal of delivering food and managing dishes requires all sub-goals to be fulfilled sequentially.

- **G2 -> G3, G4 [OR][#]**  
  Delivery can be achieved either via direct delivery (G3) or tray-based delivery (G4), with parallel options.

- **G3 -> AT1, AT2, AT3, AT4 [AND][;]**  
  Direct delivery requires sequential execution of navigation, door opening, delivery, and closing.

- **G4 -> G5, G6 [AND][FALLBACK(G5, G6)]**  
  Tray-based delivery first queries retrieval capability (G5), then handles retrieval (G6) if needed.

- **G5 -> - [Query]**  
  A leaf goal that retrieves inpatient capability data from the patient record.

- **G6 -> G6.1, G6.2, G6.3, G6.4 [AND][FALLBACK(...)]**  
  Retrieval methods are prioritized: inpatient, companion, nurse, or robot (fallback if no one is available).

- **G6.1 -> AT5, AT6 [AND][;]**  
  If the inpatient retrieves the meal, track details and alert on errors.

- **G6.2 -> AT5, AT6 [AND][;]**  
  If a companion retrieves the meal, track details and alert on errors.

- **G6.3 -> AT5, AT6 [AND][;]**  
  If a nurse retrieves the meal, track details and alert on errors.

- **G6.4 -> AT5, AT6 [AND][;]**  
  If another robot retrieves the meal, track details and alert on errors.

- **G8 -> G8.1, G8.2, G8.3 [AND][FALLBACK(...)]**  
  Dish retrieval can be unassisted (AT7), with two robots (AT7 + AT8), or with a human (AT8).

- **G8.1 -> AT7 [AND][;]**  
  Unassisted dish retrieval by the robot.

- **G8.2 -> AT7, AT8 [AND][;]**  
  Dish retrieval with two robots (one to retrieve, one to coordinate door access).

- **G8.3 -> AT8 [AND][;]**  
  Dish retrieval with human collaboration (door opening).
